**`columnFamilyHandle` is never closed in `preShutdown()`:**
```java
@Override
protected void preShutdown() {
    if (this.writeOptions != null) {
        this.writeOptions.close();
    }
    if (this.deleteOptions != null) {
        this.deleteOptions.close();
    }
    if (this.defaultCFHandle != null) {
        this.defaultCFHandle.close();
    }
    // columnFamilyHandle is missing
}
```
The `columnFamilyHandle` (the "popState" column family) is allocated in `postLoad()` but never released. This leaks a native RocksDB resource. Add:
```java
if (this.columnFamilyHandle != null) {
    this.columnFamilyHandle.close();
}
```

